<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 15: </span>Dataset statistics and benchmark coverage across TDG methods. ✓ indicates the method was originally explored and evaluated on the corresponding dataset in its original paper, demonstrating the evolution toward larger-scale TDG settings.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scalability within TDG Domain.</span> Our scalability claims are contextualized within the TDG and CDGTD domains rather than general ML standards. Table <a href="#A2.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ Appendix B Additional Discussion ‣ Scaling Up Temporal Domain Generalization via Temporal Experts Averaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> shows the evolution of benchmark coverage across TDG methods. Early methods like GI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nasery et al. (2021)</a></cite>, LSSAE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qin et al. (2022)</a></cite>, and DRAIN <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">ying Bai et al. (2022)</a></cite> were limited to small benchmarks (RMNIST, Yearbook <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al. (2022a)</a></cite>) with &lt;40K samples and minimal parameters. Recent works like EvoS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al. (2024c)</a></cite> and W-Diff <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al. (2024b)</a></cite> expanded to medium-scale benchmarks (FMoW, HuffPost, Arxiv <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al. (2022a)</a></cite>) with up to 2M samples and 66M parameters. TEA further extends this progression by introducing two new large benchmarks (CLEAR-10/100 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al. (2022)</a></cite>) and demonstrating effectiveness across the full spectrum from 30K to 2M+ samples and 29K to 66M+ parameters. This represents significant scalability advancement within the TDG field, though the scale remains modest compared to contemporary NLP/CV standards.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Notation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We denote <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> the input space, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> the label space, and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell:\mathcal{Y}^{2}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell:\mathcal{Y}^{2}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> a loss function. We have a sequence of domains <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{D_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{D_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> indexed by timestamps <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a totally ordered set representing time. Each domain <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> has a distribution <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the training (source) domains <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{D_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{D_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have timestamps <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1}&lt;t_{2}&lt;\ldots&lt;t_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1}&lt;t_{2}&lt;\ldots&lt;t_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, and corresponding distributions <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1},p_{2},\ldots,p_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1},p_{2},\ldots,p_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity, we will use <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to refer to the joint, posterior, and marginal distributions of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
We note <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}:\mathcal{X}\rightarrow\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> as the labeling function at time <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume there is no noise in the data: <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined on <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{i}\triangleq\{x\in\mathcal{X}\mid p_{i}(x)&gt;0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{i}\triangleq\{x\in\mathcal{X}\mid p_{i}(x)&gt;0\}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall(x,y)\sim p_{i},f_{i}(x)=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall(x,y)\sim p_{i},f_{i}(x)=y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Temporal Domain Generalization</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider a neural network (NN) <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,\theta):\mathcal{X}\rightarrow\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,\theta):\mathcal{X}\rightarrow\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> made of a fixed architecture <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> with weights <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>. Given observations from source domains at times <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, we seek <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> minimizing the target generalization error at a future time <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{f}&gt;t_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{f}&gt;t_{S}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{f}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim p_{f}}[\ell(f(x,\theta),y)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{f}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim p_{f}}[\ell(f(x,\theta),y)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\cdot,\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\cdot,\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> should approximate <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is challenging in the TDG setup because we only have data from earlier timestamps, which are related yet different from the future target domain.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The differences between domains at different timestamps are due to distribution shifts (i.e., the fact that <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(X,Y)\neq p_{j}(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(X,Y)\neq p_{j}(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>), which can be decomposed into:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diversity shift:</span> when marginal distributions differ over time (i.e., <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(X)\neq p_{j}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(X)\neq p_{j}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correlation shift:</span> when posterior distributions differ over time (i.e., <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(Y|X)\neq p_{j}(Y|X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(Y|X)\neq p_{j}(Y|X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}\neq f_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}\neq f_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The weights are typically learned on source domain data <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{D_{1},D_{2},\ldots,D_{S}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{D_{1},D_{2},\ldots,D_{S}\}</annotation></semantics></math> from timestamps <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{S}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{S}\}</annotation></semantics></math> (each composed of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. samples from <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(X,Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(X,Y)</annotation></semantics></math>) with a configuration <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, which contains all other configurations and sources of randomness in learning. We call <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{\mathcal{T}}=\{D_{1},D_{2},\ldots,D_{S},c\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{\mathcal{T}}=\{D_{1},D_{2},\ldots,D_{S},c\}</annotation></semantics></math> a learning procedure, and explicitly write <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta(l_{\mathcal{T}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta(l_{\mathcal{T}})</annotation></semantics></math> to refer to the weights obtained after stochastic minimization of the appropriate objective function. Specific to our TEA, we define <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{i}=\{D_{1},D_{2},\ldots,D_{S},t_{i},c\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{i}=\{D_{1},D_{2},\ldots,D_{S},t_{i},c\}</annotation></semantics></math> as a temporal expert learning procedure to get expert model <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}=\theta(l_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}=\theta(l_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> which is designed to excels on domain <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> while also using data from other domains.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Temporal Expert Averaging</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We study the benefits of combining <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> individual member weights <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}\triangleq\{\theta(l_{i})\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo>≜</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}\triangleq\{\theta(l_{i})\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> obtained from <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> different domains at timestamps <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{S}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{S}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each weight <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to an expert model that is more proficient for domain <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (though not necessarily trained exclusively on that domain).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike traditional weight averaging <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cha et al. (2021)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rame et al. (2022)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wortsman et al. (2022)</a></cite> that uses equal coefficients, for temporal domain generalization, we propose a temporally-weighted averaging scheme that assigns different importance to experts based on their relevance to the target future domain.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Temporal Expert Averaging (TEA) is defined as:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\text{TEA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\text{TEA}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq f(\cdot,\theta_{\text{TEA}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq f(\cdot,\theta_{\text{TEA}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\theta_{\text{TEA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\theta_{\text{TEA}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\triangleq\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\left(\{t_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S},\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S},t_{f}\right)\cdot\theta_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\triangleq\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\left(\{t_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S},\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S},t_{f}\right)\cdot\theta_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the coefficients <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. These coefficients are determined based on the temporal shift among the source domain experts <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and temporal information <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{t_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{t_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>TEA loss derivation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rame et al. (2022)</a></cite>, we decompose TEA’s error leveraging the similarity between WA and functional ensembling (ENS) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lakshminarayanan et al. (2017)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dietterich (2000)</a></cite>, a more traditional way to combine a collection of weights. We also use Mean Squared Error as <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity. For TDG setting, we define Temporal ENS (T-ENS) with coefficients <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\text{T-ENS}}\triangleq\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(\cdot,\theta_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\text{T-ENS}}\triangleq\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(\cdot,\theta_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#A3.EGx10" title="Lemma 1 (TWA and T-ENS). ‣ C.4 TEA loss derivation ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Analysis ‣ Scaling Up Temporal Domain Generalization via Temporal Experts Averaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> establishes that <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{TEA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{TEA}}</annotation></semantics></math> approximates <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{T-ENS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{T-ENS}}</annotation></semantics></math> to first order when <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> are close in weight space.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(TWA and T-ENS)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> with learning procedures for different temporal experts. Denoting <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\{\theta\}}=\max_{i=1}^{S}\|\theta_{i}-\theta_{\text{TEA}}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TEA</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\{\theta\}}=\max_{i=1}^{S}\|\theta_{i}-\theta_{\text{TEA}}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∀</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\text{TEA}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TEA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\text{TEA}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x)+O(\Delta^{2}_{\{\theta\}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x)+O(\Delta^{2}_{\{\theta\}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell(f_{\text{TEA}}(x),y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TEA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell(f_{\text{TEA}}(x),y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ell(f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x),y)+O(\Delta^{2}_{\{\theta\}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ell(f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x),y)+O(\Delta^{2}_{\{\theta\}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">This proof has two components:</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">to establish the functional approximation, it performs Taylor expansion of the models’ predictions at the first order.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">to establish the loss approximation, it performs Taylor expansion of the loss at the first order.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Functional approximation<span id="A3.SS4.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> With a Taylor expansion at the first order of the models’ predictions w.r.t. parameters <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\theta_{i}}=f_{\text{TEA}}+\nabla f|_{\text{TEA}}\Delta_{i}+O\left(\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\theta_{i}}=f_{\text{TEA}}+\nabla f|_{\text{TEA}}\Delta_{i}+O\left(\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\text{T-ENS}}-f_{\text{TEA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\text{T-ENS}}-f_{\text{TEA}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\nabla f|_{\text{TEA}}\Delta_{i}+\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}O\left(\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\nabla f|_{\text{TEA}}\Delta_{i}+\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}O\left(\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}=\theta_{i}-\theta_{\text{TWA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>TWA</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=\theta_{i}-\theta_{\text{TWA}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that unlike in the equal weighting case, we don’t have <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{S}\Delta_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{S}\Delta_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for weighted averaging. Instead, we have <math id="A3.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\Delta_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\Delta_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\text{T-ENS}}-f_{\text{TEA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\text{T-ENS}}-f_{\text{TEA}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\nabla f|_{\text{TEA}}\Delta_{i}+\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}O\left(\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi><msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\nabla f|_{\text{TEA}}\Delta_{i}+\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}O\left(\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\nabla f|_{\text{TWA}}\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\Delta_{i}+O\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mtext>TWA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\nabla f|_{\text{TWA}}\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\Delta_{i}+O\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\|\Delta_{i}\|^{2}_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}\leq\Delta_{\{\theta\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}\leq\Delta_{\{\theta\}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\text{T-ENS}}-f_{\text{TEA}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\text{T-ENS}}-f_{\text{TEA}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\Delta_{\{\theta\}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\Delta_{\{\theta\}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\left(\Delta_{\{\theta\}}^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\left(\Delta_{\{\theta\}}^{2}\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\left(\Delta_{\{\theta\}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\left(\Delta_{\{\theta\}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Loss approximation.</span> With a Taylor expansion at the zeroth order of the loss w.r.t. its first input and injecting the functional approximation:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell(f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x);y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell(f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x);y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ell(f_{\text{TWA}}(x);y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TWA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ell(f_{\text{TWA}}(x);y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+O(\|f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x)-f_{\text{TEA}}(x)\|_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+O(\|f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x)-f_{\text{TEA}}(x)\|_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell(f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x);y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell(f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x);y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ell(f_{\text{TEA}}(x);y)+O\left(\Delta_{\{\theta\}}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ell(f_{\text{TEA}}(x);y)+O\left(\Delta_{\{\theta\}}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Bias-variance-covariance-locality Decomposition for TEA</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We can derive the following decomposition of TEA’s expected test error in the future domain. The expectation is over the joint distribution describing the <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> learning procedures <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{l_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{l_{i}\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. (<span id="A3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note that in the temporal domain generalization (TDG) setting, models from different timestamps may have different biases and variances due to the evolution of data distributions over time. This temporal heterogeneity is a key characteristic that distinguishes TDG from standard DG.</span>)</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bias-variance-covariance-locality decomposition for temporal weight averaging)<span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Denoting <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}_{i}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{l_{i}}[f(x,\theta(l_{i}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}_{i}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{l_{i}}[f(x,\theta(l_{i}))]</annotation></semantics></math> as the expected prediction of an expert model for timestamp <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{f}=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim p_{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{f}=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim p_{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{l}=\{l_{1},\ldots,l_{S}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐥</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{l}=\{l_{1},\ldots,l_{S}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected generalization error on future domain <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{TWA}}=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\cdot\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TWA</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{TWA}}=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\cdot\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> over the joint distribution of the learning procedures is:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[\mathcal{E}_{f}(\theta_{\text{TEA}})]=\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\mathcal{B}+\mathcal{V}+\mathcal{C}\right]+O(\bar{\Delta}^{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TEA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[\mathcal{E}_{f}(\theta_{\text{TEA}})]=\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\mathcal{B}+\mathcal{V}+\mathcal{C}\right]+O(\bar{\Delta}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{B}=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\cdot\text{bias}_{i}\right)^{2},\ \text{bias}_{i}=y-\bar{f}_{i}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">bias</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">bias</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{B}=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\cdot\text{bias}_{i}\right)^{2},\ \text{bias}_{i}=y-\bar{f}_{i}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{V}=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\cdot\text{var}_{i},\ \text{var}_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{l_{i}}\left[dev_{i}^{2}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">var</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">var</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{V}=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\cdot\text{var}_{i},\ \text{var}_{i}=\mathbb{E}_{l_{i}}\left[dev_{i}^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{C}=\sum_{i\neq j}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\text{cov}_{i,j},\ \text{cov}_{i,j}=\mathbb{E}_{\{l_{i},l_{j}\}}\left[dev_{i}\cdot dev_{j}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">cov</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">cov</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{C}=\sum_{i\neq j}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\text{cov}_{i,j},\ \text{cov}_{i,j}=\mathbb{E}_{\{l_{i},l_{j}\}}\left[dev_{i}\cdot dev_{j}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle with\ dev_{i}=f(x,\theta(l_{i}))-\bar{f}_{i}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle with\ dev_{i}=f(x,\theta(l_{i}))-\bar{f}_{i}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{\Delta}^{2}=\mathbb{E}[\Delta^{2}_{\{\theta\}}]\text{ with }\Delta_{\{\theta\}}=\max_{i=1}^{S}\|\theta_{i}-\theta_{\text{TWA}}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> with </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munderover><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">TWA</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{\Delta}^{2}=\mathbb{E}[\Delta^{2}_{\{\theta\}}]\text{ with }\Delta_{\{\theta\}}=\max_{i=1}^{S}\|\theta_{i}-\theta_{\text{TWA}}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rame et al. (2022)</a></cite>, we use the he bias-variance decomposition in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kohavi et al. (1996)</a></cite> with <math id="A3.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\text{T-ENS}}\triangleq\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(\cdot,\theta(l_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">≜</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\text{T-ENS}}\triangleq\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(\cdot,\theta(l_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math> to decompose the expected generalization error:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[\mathcal{E}_{f}(\{\theta(l_{i})\}_{i=1}^{S})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[\mathcal{E}_{f}(\{\theta(l_{i})\}_{i=1}^{S})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{f}[\text{Bias}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|(x,y)\}^{2}+\text{Var}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|x\}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Bias</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{f}[\text{Bias}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|(x,y)\}^{2}+\text{Var}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|x\}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where bias term becomes:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Bias}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|(x,y)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Bias</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Bias}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|(x,y)\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=y-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(x,\theta(l_{i}))\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=y-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(x,\theta(l_{i}))\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=y-\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[f(x,\theta(l_{i}))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=y-\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[f(x,\theta(l_{i}))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=y-\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\bar{f}_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=y-\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\bar{f}_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}(y-\bar{f}_{i}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}(y-\bar{f}_{i}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\text{bias}_{i}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>bias</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\text{bias}_{i}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the squared bias term is:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Bias}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|(x,y)\}^{2}=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\text{bias}_{i}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Bias</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>bias</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Bias}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|(x,y)\}^{2}=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\text{bias}_{i}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the variance term, denoting <math id="A3.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{dev}_{i}=f(x,\theta(l_{i}))-\bar{f}_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>dev</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{dev}_{i}=f(x,\theta(l_{i}))-\bar{f}_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A3.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:187.5pt;height:132pt;vertical-align:-63.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<p id="A3.SS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"><math id="A3.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{aligned} &amp;\text{Var}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|x\}\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(x,\theta(l_{i}))-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(x,\theta(l_{i}))\right]\right)^{2}\right]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}(f(x,\theta(l_{i}))-\bar{f}_{i}(x))\right)^{2}\right]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{S}\sum_{j=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\cdot\text{dev}_{i}\cdot\text{dev}_{j}\right]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[\text{dev}_{i}^{2}]+\sum_{i\neq j}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[\text{dev}_{i}\cdot\text{dev}_{j}]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\text{var}_{i}+\sum_{i\neq j}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\text{cov}_{i,j}\end{aligned}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>dev</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>dev</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mtext>dev</mtext><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐥</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>dev</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>dev</mtext><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>var</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>cov</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{aligned} &amp;\text{Var}\{f_{\text{T-ENS}}|x\}\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(x,\theta(l_{i}))-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}f(x,\theta(l_{i}))\right]\right)^{2}\right]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}(f(x,\theta(l_{i}))-\bar{f}_{i}(x))\right)^{2}\right]\\
&amp;=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{S}\sum_{j=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\cdot\text{dev}_{i}\cdot\text{dev}_{j}\right]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[\text{dev}_{i}^{2}]+\sum_{i\neq j}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{l}}[\text{dev}_{i}\cdot\text{dev}_{j}]\\
&amp;=\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\text{var}_{i}+\sum_{i\neq j}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\text{cov}_{i,j}\end{aligned}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</span></div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS5.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Combination with Lemma 1</span> We recall that per our adapted Lemma 1:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell(f_{\text{TEA}}(x),y)=\ell(f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x),y)+O(\Delta^{2}_{\{\theta\}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext>T-ENS</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell(f_{\text{TEA}}(x),y)=\ell(f_{\text{T-ENS}}(x),y)+O(\Delta^{2}_{\{\theta\}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Taking the expectation over the learning procedures and combining all terms:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{f}(\theta_{\text{TEA}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>TEA</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{E}_{f}(\theta_{\text{TEA}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\text{bias}_{i}\right)^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>bias</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\text{bias}_{i}\right)^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\text{var}_{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>var</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\text{var}_{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\sum_{i\neq j}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\text{ cov}_{i,j}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext> cov</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\sum_{i\neq j}\alpha_{i}\alpha_{j}\text{ cov}_{i,j}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+O(\bar{\Delta}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+O(\bar{\Delta}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.p6.3" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.6 </span>Theoretical Insights for TEA</h3>

<div id="A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From Equation <a href="#A3.E11" title="In Proposition 1 (Bias-variance-covariance-locality decomposition for temporal weight averaging). ‣ C.5 Bias-variance-covariance-locality Decomposition for TEA ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Analysis ‣ Scaling Up Temporal Domain Generalization via Temporal Experts Averaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, we can see that generalization error can be reduced by minimizing bias <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, variance <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, covariance <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, and locality <math id="A3.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Delta}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Delta}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, due to the complexity of real-world data and models, finding an optimal analytical solution is nearly impossible. Nevertheless, similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rame et al. (2022)</a></cite>, we can derive practical insights for designing TEA by analyzing the relationships between these four terms, model properties, and averaging coefficients.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Insight 1</span> <span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Tradeoff between Functional Diversity and Parameter Similarity among Experts.</span> Covariance <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> reduction necessitates functional diversity among experts, while the locality constraint <math id="A3.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Delta}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Delta}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> demands parameter similarity among experts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The covariance term increases when the predictions of <math id="A3.SS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f(\cdot,\theta(l_{i}))\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f(\cdot,\theta(l_{i}))\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> are correlated, suggesting that DiWA’s <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rame et al. (2022)</a></cite> approach to reduce covariance by encouraging functional diversity remains effective. However, the locality term <math id="A3.SS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Delta}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Delta}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously constrains the weights to remain close in parameter space. This tradeoff suggests that when training these expert models, we should find an appropriate balance between encouraging diverse predictions and maintaining parameter similarity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Insight 2</span> <span id="A3.SS6.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Tradeoff between Bias and Variance via Averaging Coefficients.</span> Reducing variance <math id="A3.SS6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> requires averaging weights evenly, while reducing bias <math id="A3.SS6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> demands concentrating coefficients on experts with lower bias magnitudes on future data.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Insight 2 is obtained by introducing 2 assumptions specific to the TDG for further discussion about bias and variance.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Ordered Bias Magnitudes)<span id="Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The models can be ordered by expected bias magnitudes on future domains such that <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{bias}_{m_{1}}^{2}\right]\geq\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{bias}_{m_{1}}^{2}\right]\geq\cdots\geq\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{bias}_{m_{S}}^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">bias</mtext><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">bias</mtext><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">bias</mtext><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{bias}_{m_{1}}^{2}\right]\geq\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{bias}_{m_{1}}^{2}\right]\geq\cdots\geq\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{bias}_{m_{S}}^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{m_{j}\}_{j=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{m_{j}\}_{j=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> being a permutation of <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{i\}_{i=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{i\}_{i=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Equal Variance Experts)<span id="Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The variance of each expert’s prediction is equal across all experts, such that <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{var}_{i}\right]=v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">var</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{var}_{i}\right]=v</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2,...,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2,...,M\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Optimal Averaging Coefficients for Bias Minimization</span>)<span id="Thmlemma2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let the bias of model <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> be:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b_{i}(x,y)=\operatorname{bias}_{i}(x,y),\sigma_{i}^{2}:=\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[b_{i}^{2}\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>bias</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b_{i}(x,y)=\operatorname{bias}_{i}(x,y),\sigma_{i}^{2}:=\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[b_{i}^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and define the root-mean-square magnitude:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma_{i}=\sqrt{\sigma_{i}^{2}}\quad(i=1,\ldots,S)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msqrt></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma_{i}=\sqrt{\sigma_{i}^{2}}\quad(i=1,\ldots,S).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">According to Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Ordered Bias Magnitudes). ‣ C.6 Theoretical Insights for TEA ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Analysis ‣ Scaling Up Temporal Domain Generalization via Temporal Experts Averaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, magnitudes are ordered <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{m_{1}}\geq\sigma_{m_{2}}\geq\cdots\geq\sigma_{m_{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{m_{1}}\geq\sigma_{m_{2}}\geq\cdots\geq\sigma_{m_{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{m_{j}\}_{j=1}^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{m_{j}\}_{j=1}^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is a permutation of <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\ldots,S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\ldots,S\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For convex weights <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}\in\Delta^{S}:=\{\alpha_{i}\geq 0,\,\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛂</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}\in\Delta^{S}:=\{\alpha_{i}\geq 0,\,\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the combined bias loss:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L(\boldsymbol{\alpha}):=\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}b_{i}\right)^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L(\boldsymbol{\alpha}):=\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}b_{i}\right)^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <span id="Thmlemma2.p1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">no information</span> is available on the pairwise bias covariances <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ij}:=\mathbb{E}_{f}[b_{i}b_{j}]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ij}:=\mathbb{E}_{f}[b_{i}b_{j}],</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i\neq j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i\neq j)</annotation></semantics></math>, then the minimax problem:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\boldsymbol{\alpha}\in\Delta^{S}}\;\max_{\Sigma\text{ s.t. }\operatorname{diag}(\Sigma)=\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{2}}L(\boldsymbol{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.447em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> s.t. </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝝈</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\boldsymbol{\alpha}\in\Delta^{S}}\;\max_{\Sigma\text{ s.t. }\operatorname{diag}(\Sigma)=\boldsymbol{\sigma}^{2}}L(\boldsymbol{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is solved by:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{\alpha^{\star}_{m_{S}}=1,\quad\alpha^{\star}_{i}=0\;\text{for}\;i\neq m_{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for</mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{\alpha^{\star}_{m_{S}}=1,\quad\alpha^{\star}_{i}=0\;\text{for}\;i\neq m_{S}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\boldsymbol{\alpha}^{\star})=\sigma_{m_{S}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝛂</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\boldsymbol{\alpha}^{\star})=\sigma_{m_{S}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can write <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\boldsymbol{\alpha})=\boldsymbol{\alpha}^{\top}\Sigma\boldsymbol{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜶</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\boldsymbol{\alpha})=\boldsymbol{\alpha}^{\top}\Sigma\boldsymbol{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> with unknown positive-semidefinite matrix <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ii}=\sigma_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ii}=\sigma_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Sigma_{ij}|\leq\sigma_{i}\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Sigma_{ij}|\leq\sigma_{i}\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. The worst case occurs when all covariances reach the extreme value <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ij}=\sigma_{i}\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ij}=\sigma_{i}\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\Sigma}L(\boldsymbol{\alpha})=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\sigma_{i}\right)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜶</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\Sigma}L(\boldsymbol{\alpha})=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\sigma_{i}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\alpha_{i}\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\alpha_{i}\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex combination of the ordered set <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{m_{j}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{m_{j}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, its minimum over the simplex <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is attained by placing all weight on the smallest RMS magnitude <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{m_{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{m_{S}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives the stated <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and the minimax value <math id="A3.SS6.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(\boldsymbol{\alpha}^{\star})=\sigma_{m_{S}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(\boldsymbol{\alpha}^{\star})=\sigma_{m_{S}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimal Averaging Coefficients for Variance Minimization)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the variance term with equal variances <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{var}_{i}\right]=v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">var</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\text{var}_{i}\right]=v</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\ldots,S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\ldots,S\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\mathcal{V}\right]=v\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{f}\left[\mathcal{V}\right]=v\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For averaging coefficients <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\boldsymbol{\alpha}\in\Delta^{S}:=\{\alpha_{i}\geq 0,\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛂</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>S</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\alpha}\in\Delta^{S}:=\{\alpha_{i}\geq 0,\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the variance term is minimized when weights are distributed equally across all models:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boxed{\alpha_{i}^{\star}=\frac{1}{S}\text{ for all }i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boxed{\alpha_{i}^{\star}=\frac{1}{S}\text{ for all }i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with optimal variance <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\cdot\frac{1}{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\cdot\frac{1}{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS6.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We seek to minimize <math id="A3.SS6.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to the constraints <math id="A3.SS6.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS6.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\right)^{2}\leq S\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\right)^{2}\leq S\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">with equality if and only if all <math id="A3.SS6.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are equal. Since <math id="A3.SS6.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\right)^{2}\leq S\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}\right)^{2}\leq S\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS6.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">which implies <math id="A3.SS6.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\geq\frac{1}{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{S}\alpha_{i}^{2}\geq\frac{1}{S}</annotation></semantics></math>. Equality is achieved when <math id="A3.SS6.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{i}=\frac{1}{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{i}=\frac{1}{S}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS6.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, giving the optimal solution.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p8.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Optimal Averaging Coefficients for Bias Minimization). ‣ C.6 Theoretical Insights for TEA ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Analysis ‣ Scaling Up Temporal Domain Generalization via Temporal Experts Averaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> indicates that optimizing the bias term requires concentrating weight on experts with smaller bias magnitude on future domains, while Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Optimal Averaging Coefficients for Variance Minimization). ‣ C.6 Theoretical Insights for TEA ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Analysis ‣ Scaling Up Temporal Domain Generalization via Temporal Experts Averaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> suggests that minimizing variance requires the opposite approach—distributing weight as evenly as possible across all experts. This creates a fundamental tradeoff between bias and variance in the selection of averaging coefficients.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS6.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Discussion about Assumptions.</span> Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (Ordered Bias Magnitudes). ‣ C.6 Theoretical Insights for TEA ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Analysis ‣ Scaling Up Temporal Domain Generalization via Temporal Experts Averaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is similar to the smooth distribution shift assumption used by most prior TDG methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">ying Bai et al. (2022)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zeng et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nasery et al. (2021)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al. (2024b)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al. (2024c)</a></cite>, allowing us to model distribution change and leverage temporal information to predict future parameter or feature. Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2 (Equal Variance Experts). ‣ C.6 Theoretical Insights for TEA ‣ Appendix C Theoretical Analysis ‣ Scaling Up Temporal Domain Generalization via Temporal Experts Averaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is reasonable when all experts share the same architecture, optimization procedure and hyperparameters, differing only in the specific temporal domains they’ve been optimized to excel in.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Results</h2>

<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.26045v1/figs/coeffs/huffpost_coeff.png" id="A4.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/234;" width="476" height="234" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Huffpost.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.26045v1/figs/coeffs/arxiv.png" id="A4.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/234;" width="476" height="234" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Arxiv.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.26045v1/figs/coeffs/yearbook_coeff.png" id="A4.F6.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/237;" width="476" height="237" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Yearbook.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.26045v1/figs/coeffs/rmnist.png" id="A4.F6.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/237;" width="476" height="237" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>RMNIST.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.26045v1/figs/coeffs/fmow_coeff.png" id="A4.F6.sf5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/237;" width="476" height="237" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(e) </span>FMoW.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf6" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.26045v1/figs/coeffs/clear10_coeff.png" id="A4.F6.sf6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/234;" width="476" height="234" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(f) </span>CLEAR-10.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf7" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.26045v1/figs/coeffs/clear100_coeff.png" id="A4.F6.sf7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/234;" width="476" height="234" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(g) </span>CLEAR-100.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Visualization of averaging coefficients and accuracies of experts on target domain <math id="A4.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{S+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{S+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We show the coefficients vs. <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{S+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{S+1}</annotation></semantics></math> accuracy across all benchmarks in Figure <a href="#A4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix D Additional Results ‣ Scaling Up Temporal Domain Generalization via Temporal Experts Averaging" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. The results reveal diverse performance patterns among experts, with a clear temporal trend: experts trained on earlier domains consistently achieve lower accuracy on the subsequent domain. This systematic pattern demonstrates that expert functionality undergoes structured evolution throughout the finetuning process. In addition, our temporal trajectory forecasting approach successfully identifies this pattern and assigns higher coefficients to experts that demonstrate superior performance on future domains, effectively leveraging the temporal dynamics to improve expert selection and utilization.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
